Rules for Declaring Variables in Java:
1. Every variable must have a data type.
2. A variable name must start with a letter, underscore (_), or dollar sign ($).
3. A variable name cannot start with a digit.
4. Variable names cannot contain spaces.
5. Java keywords cannot be used as variable names.
6. Variable names are case-sensitive.
7. Special characters are not allowed except _ and $.
8. A variable must be declared before it is used.
9. Local variables must be initialized before use.
10. Multiple variables of the same data type can be declared in one statement.

